change:
  id: CHG-002
  title: Live mutation loop policy
  status: accepted
  intent: Resolve the first live provider, behavior-first mutation contract, S-expression internal representation, realization boundary, crossover stance, promotion target, reviewer evidence behavior and deterministic fitness policy before broad implementation.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - DOM-001
    - SYS-001
    - CON-001
    - ARCH-001
    - RISK-001
    - RISK-002
    - Q-001
    - Q-002
    - Q-003
    - Q-004
    - Q-005
    - Q-006
    - Q-007

deltas:
  - op: MODIFIED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: The system evaluates live model-proposed behavioral implementation mutations through explicit TOON contract envelopes, S-expression internal mutation IR, realization, review, promotion and scoring policies without allowing model approval authority.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: live model proposal mode is configured for the CLI
        then: provider-specific LangChain4j construction stays in the adapters/langchain4j package and deterministic code receives only the MutationProposer port
        and:
          - no live model call is attempted unless provider, model and credentials are explicitly configured
      - id: S2
        when: the model proposes a targeted mutation contract with behavioral hypothesis, operator, loci, bounds and required evidence
        then: deterministic validation canonicalizes it to S-expression mutation IR and accepts only bounded contracts before candidate creation
        and:
          - unsupported operators, unsafe loci, excessive change budgets and authority-bearing fields are rejected
          - the mutation operator is one of the closed initial enum values
      - id: S3
        when: a candidate produces checks, benchmark evidence and optional reviewer evidence
        then: deterministic scoring evaluates candidate phenotype evidence with hard gates and configured objective weights to produce FitnessResult
        and:
          - all required deterministic behavior cases must pass before weighted scoring can promote
          - model-supplied approval, score, rollback or promotion fields are ignored or rejected before scoring
      - id: S4
        when: the deterministic policy promotes a candidate
        then: promotion records SQLite metadata and updates a local promoted candidate Git ref without merging main or deploying
        and:
          - discarded candidates remain auditable until an explicit retention policy exists
      - id: S5
        when: actor review tooling is unavailable during evaluation
        then: the loop records unavailable review evidence and follows deterministic required-or-advisory reviewer policy
        and:
          - unavailable review is never treated as a successful review
      - id: S6
        when: crossover is requested for evaluated parent candidates
        then: the system creates a conceptual trait-recombination proposal whose child uses the closed mutation operator enum rather than merging raw diffs
        and:
          - parent traits are selected from recorded evidence and the child contract remains bounded to one primary locus
      - id: S7
        when: a mutation operator is selected for the next loop
        then: the loop derives default bounds, required evidence and fitness dimensions from the operator contract
        and:
          - model output cannot redefine operator semantics during evaluation
      - id: S8
        when: hill-climb or exploratory-leap is selected
        then: the loop records search posture, parent candidate, objective focus and risk budget before realization
        and:
          - both operators still use deterministic fitness gates for selection

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: cli/LiveLoopConfigurationAcceptanceTest.rejectsLiveModeWithoutExplicitProviderModelAndCredentials
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: adapters/OpenAiMutationProposerFactoryTest.constructsOpenAiChatModelOnlyInsideAdapter
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: deterministic/MutationContractCanonicalizerTest.emitsStableSExpressionMutationIr
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: deterministic/MutationContractValidatorTest.acceptsBoundedTargetedMutationContract
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: deterministic/MutationContractValidatorTest.rejectsUnsupportedOperatorUnsafeLociOrExcessiveBudget
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: deterministic/PhenotypeFitnessScorerTest.appliesHardGatesBeforeWeightedObjectives
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: deterministic/PhenotypeFitnessScorerTest.requiresAllRequiredBehaviorCasesBeforePromotion
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: deterministic/MutationEvaluationLoopAcceptanceTest.rejectsModelSuppliedApprovalOrScoreBeforeEvaluation
    layer: component
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: adapters/GitPromotionSinkIntegrationTest.promotesCandidateToLocalPromotedRefWithoutTouchingMain
    layer: component-integration
  - scenario: S5
    test_id: deterministic/ReviewerEvidencePolicyTest.recordsUnavailableActorReviewWithoutPassingReview
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S6
    test_id: deterministic/ConceptualCrossoverPolicyTest.createsChildContractWithClosedMutationOperatorFromEvidenceBackedTraits
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S7
    test_id: deterministic/MutationOperatorTypeTest.mapsOperatorToDefaultBoundsEvidenceAndFitnessDimensions
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S8
    test_id: deterministic/SearchPosturePolicyTest.recordsHillClimbAndExploratoryLeapControls
    layer: unit

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: document source-backed live-loop policy proposal
    status: completed
  - id: T1b
    slice: document mutation and crossover theory plus repository mutation-contract skill
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: add CLI live-provider configuration contract and OpenAI LangChain4j factory
    status: pending
  - id: T3
    slice: add S-expression mutation contract canonicalizer and bounded contract validator
    status: completed
  - id: T3b
    slice: add closed mutation operator enum and deterministic operator defaults
    status: completed
  - id: T3c
    slice: add search posture policy for hill-climb and exploratory-leap operators
    status: completed
  - id: T3d
    slice: add TOON mutation contract envelope parser feeding the canonicalizer
    status: pending
  - id: T4
    slice: implement deterministic fitness scorer with hard gates and weights
    status: completed
  - id: T4b
    slice: pass the accepted mutation contract and a required-evidence channel into the scorer so declared hard gates are enforced, not just declared
    status: completed
    note: delivered by CHG-014. The scorer now has a four-argument entry point taking the contract and a typed RequiredEvidenceResult channel, enforcing declared ids as canonical subject-invariant integrity gates in addition to the structural gates. The wired path does not use it, so RISK-002 stays open; that remainder is T4c
  - id: T4c
    slice: migrate MutationEvaluationLoop from Mutation onto MutationContract and thread the accepted contract through FitnessScorer and PhenotypeBridgeScorer, so the contract-aware scorer entry point is the one the wired promotion path reaches
    status: completed
    note: delivered by CHG-019, in a different shape than written. The loop still proposes a Mutation; what it now carries is an operator-declared MutationContract alongside it, because nothing produces a contract from a proposer and T3d's envelope parser needs a TOON reader that does not exist. The FitnessScorer port takes the contract, so a declared required_evidence id gates a live promotion and RISK-002 narrows to the contractless path, which declares nothing
    note: this is the loop-side half of RISK-002 and the only remaining work before that risk can close. Until CHG-014 it existed only as a HANDOFF backlog line and a CHG-005 risk note, not as a tracked task. The FitnessScorer port takes (Candidate, EvaluationEvidence) and cannot carry a contract, so the port changes with it
  - id: T5
    slice: implement local promoted Git ref plus SQLite promotion metadata
    status: pending
  - id: T6
    slice: encode actor-review evidence fallback as deterministic evaluation evidence
    status: pending
  - id: T7
    slice: add conceptual crossover contract generation behind deterministic parent evidence filters
    status: completed
    note: deterministic child-contract generation only; loop integration and diff crossover remain deferred

non_goals:
  - OpenSearch or vector storage
  - AST mutation
  - LSP integration
  - distributed workers
  - automatic production deployment
  - direct promotion to main
  - model-authored fitness score or model approval channel
  - raw code-diff crossover

risks:
  - RISK-001 model self-approval if live provider output can bypass deterministic validation or scoring
  - treating realization shape as the mutation would bias the search toward edit mechanics instead of workflow behavior
  - raw crossover over LLM-authored diffs can combine two nondeterministic edits into an unauditable child
  - benchmark budgets may be too crude until baseline and candidate benchmarks are captured in one comparable run
  - local promoted refs are auditable but may not satisfy future protected-branch governance
